{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Seam guards: step-registry membership, gate-YAML resolution, and headroom for the unguarded hot files\n\n## Context / Problem\nWith the per-FUNCTION ratchet declined by the operator (blast radius: 62 functions over 120 lines\nacross six subsystems), SEAM TESTS are the only remaining structural defence against module regrowth.\nChange 1484 added `< 700` headroom assertions for `gate_dispatch.py` and `orchestrator.py`, and those\ntwo are the comfortable files today BECAUSE of it. The files that hurt now have no such guard.\n\nTHREE CONCRETE GAPS, all verified in the tree:\n\n**1. No headroom guard on the files that need it.** `tests/unit/test_gate_dispatch_seam.py:26-29`\npins exactly four paths — `gate_dispatch.py`, `plan_review_recovery.py`, `orchestrator.py`,\n`context_assembly.py`. `plan_review/workflow_ops.py` (794 LOC) and `llm/config.py` (793) appear\nNOWHERE. `tests/unit/test_structured_run_seam.py:31-33` does the same for `runner.py` only.\n\n**2. A guard whose stated premise is STALE.**\n`test_gate_dispatch_seam.py:46-53` asserts `gate_dispatch.py < 700` and justifies itself with\n\"adding an argument at its three finalize_verdict call sites is not a build break\" (`:52`). Change\n1484 MOVED those three sites to `workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`. VERIFIED: the five\n`finalize_verdict` sites are now `plan_review/workflow_ops.py:223` and `:760`, and\n`plan_review_recovery.py:223`, `:297`, `:336` — ZERO remain in `gate_dispatch.py`. The assertion still\npasses (527 LOC) but guards a premise that no longer holds, and the two sites that DO need protection\nsit in the unguarded file. The prose at `:4` and at `plan_review_recovery.py:8` is stale the same way.\n\n**3. An unregistered workflow step cannot be caught statically — the worst of the three.**\n`@register_step` writes into the process-global `STEP_REGISTRY` as an IMPORT SIDE EFFECT\n(`workflow/executor.py:180`, assignment at `:203`). Registration depends on a single import chain:\n`workflow/steps.py:341` imports `plan_review.workflow_ops`, which at `:45` imports\n`prerequisite_workflow_ops` purely for its side effect. Nothing asserts either import survives — a\nroutine \"remove unused import\" cleanup would silently unregister\n`plan_review_prerequisite_verify_inputs`. THIS HAZARD IS ALREADY LATENT TODAY, before any refactor.\nAnd no layer catches it:\n * the workflow schema treats `uses` as a free-form string (`workflow/schema.py:331`, `:372`);\n * `lint_workflow` treats an unknown step as UNKNOWN and SKIPS validation BY DESIGN\n   (`workflow/lint_refs.py:441-447`, `executor.py:214-216`), so the lint-clean test still passes;\n * `tests/unit/workflow/test_contracts.py:186` LOOKS like a completeness guard but iterates\n   `STEP_REGISTRY` itself — an op that vanished from the registry is invisible to it.\nOnly a runtime `WorkflowError` (`executor.py:676`) catches it, and only for ops on an executed path.\n\n## Approach\nAdd the guards, and land this BEFORE any relocation so the guards exist independently of the refactor\nthey protect — the refactor must not be the change that also introduces its own safety net.\n\nTHE THRESHOLD IS STAGED, and an earlier draft of this plan contradicted itself on it (Approach said\n`< 700`, Testing said `< 800`) — resolved here in favour of staging, because the two files this guard\ncovers are ABOVE 700 TODAY (`workflow_ops.py` 794, `config.py` 793). A `< 700` assertion would land\nRED, so this ticket asserts `< 800` (the hard cap — still a real guard: it catches the next commit\nthat would breach) and the sibling EXTRACTION tickets tighten their own file to `< 700` in the same\nchange that creates the headroom. That keeps every ticket independently landable.\n\n`< 700` remains the POLICY number the extractions must reach, and it is calibrated rather than\narbitrary: it matches both existing seam tests, and 100 lines of headroom absorbs observed change\nsize — median per-commit delta to `workflow_ops.py` over its last 20 commits ~+10, mean ~+18,\np90 ~+45, worst +185 (`f373cf4a6e`). Do NOT assert tighter than 700 even after the extraction:\nencoding a refactor's OUTCOME turns the guard into a change-detector that fails on the next\nlegitimate commit while saying nothing about correctness.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/` — a new plan-review workflow-ops seam test; the registry-membership and\n  gate-YAML-resolution guards.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_dispatch_seam.py` — correct the stale rationale to name the file that now holds\n  the call sites.\n  (`plan_review_recovery.py` is deliberately NOT in scope — its docstring was verified accurate.)\n\n## Testing\n- assert the exact expected plan-review step-registry membership after importing\n  `rebar.llm.workflow.steps`: the eight ops in `workflow_ops` plus\n  `plan_review_prerequisite_verify_inputs`. Prove it bites by deleting the `:45` import locally.\n- assert every `uses:` in `gates/plan-review.yaml` resolves in `STEP_REGISTRY`. Location-independent by\n  construction, so it survives every future move — `plan_review_prerequisite_verify_inputs` already\n  lives in another module while referenced at `plan-review.yaml:136`, which is the working proof.\n- headroom assertions for `plan_review/workflow_ops.py` and `llm/config.py`. These will pass only\n  AFTER their sibling extraction tickets land, so this ticket asserts the weak `< 800` form now and the\n  extraction tickets tighten to `< 700` — otherwise this ticket lands red.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] a test asserts the full expected plan-review step-registry membership, and it FAILS when the\n      registration import at `workflow_ops.py:45` is removed\n- [ ] a test asserts every `uses:` in `gates/plan-review.yaml` is present in `STEP_REGISTRY`\n- [ ] a test asserts a headroom bound for `plan_review/workflow_ops.py` and for `llm/config.py`,\n      at `< 800` — the staged form, since both exceed 700 until their extraction tickets land\n- [ ] `test_gate_dispatch_seam.py`'s assertion message no longer claims `gate_dispatch.py` holds\n      `finalize_verdict` call sites (it holds zero); it names the files that do —\n      `plan_review_recovery.py` (3) and `plan_review/workflow_ops.py` (2)\n- [ ] no production behaviour changes: this ticket adds tests and corrects comments only"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785565351450782001,"uuid":"e09dabba-d3a2-4bef-9130-980396708449"}